From: ManicardiMatteo87 <manicardi.matteo87@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:34:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] research(motion): P3b, the release that builds a
 segment plan keeps the probe at the accepted scale

A STAND from PRONE builds the DEPLOY and LIFT plans in the release that ends
the preceding segment, and the attenuated compensation of that release then
solved twice (probe at the last accepted scale, then the projection). In the
plan release (planned_ and segmentStartUs_ == now, existing state) the probe
is kept when its scale does not exceed the projection: a correction no larger
than the attenuation allows, for that one release; the next release takes
the projection as before. A shrinking projection still solves at once.

Host rig (64 scenarios): no RAW frame differs, applied correction within
0.04 mrad. QEMU (fixture scenario): ALIGN->DEPLOY release 1 606 k -> below
1 208 k instructions with E1+P3a. Research candidate, not validated on
hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/simple/SimpleMotion.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/simple/SimpleMotion.cpp b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/simple/SimpleMotion.cpp
index 935c2c9..8eff24f 100644
--- a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/simple/SimpleMotion.cpp
+++ b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/simple/SimpleMotion.cpp
@@ -1492,7 +1492,12 @@ void SimpleMotion::compensate(LocomotionFrame& f,uint64_t now){
   // same Motion epoch, not a second timer or a servo acceleration controller.
   const double envelope=quinticTimeLaw(std::fmin(1.,double(now-imuStartUs_)/1e6),1).progress;
   const double projection=probe.valid?envelope/std::sqrt(1+4*sum):0;
-  if(projection>0&&std::abs(projection-trialScale)<=.02*projection&&pointSafe(probe)&&contains(box,probe)){
+  // P3b (P0 peaks, 16/11): the release that has just built a segment plan (beginPlan,
+  // ~0.5-1.1 M instructions) keeps the probe at the last accepted scale when that scale
+  // does not exceed the projection: a correction no larger than the attenuation allows,
+  // for that one release; the next release takes the projection as before.
+  const bool planRelease=planned_&&segmentStartUs_==now&&trialScale<=projection;
+  if(projection>0&&(planRelease||std::abs(projection-trialScale)<=.02*projection)&&pointSafe(probe)&&contains(box,probe)){
     keep(probe);rollCorrection_=roll;pitchCorrection_=pitch;imuLimited_=projection<.999;if(imuLimited_)imuReason_="ATTENUATED";return;}
   for(unsigned trial=0;trial<5&&projection>0;++trial){const double scale=projection*std::ldexp(1.,-static_cast<int>(trial));
     const auto q=solve(scale,probe.valid?probe:f.target);
